# configure/networking.md: NETWORK SETTINGS, the Wi-Fi picker, a saved
# network's dialog and SAVED NETWORKS. Needs the stand-in wifictl (README).
# NETWORK SETTINGS is seven presses up from the MAIN MENU's top row (the
# unmarked stop, BACK, QUIT, SYSTEM SETTINGS, UPDATES & DOWNLOADS, SCRAPER,
# NETWORK SETTINGS); on
# it, WI-FI NETWORK is five presses down from IP ADDRESS and MANAGE SAVED
# NETWORKS two more. In the picker the stand-in lists Home Wi-Fi (in use)
# first and Cafe (saved) third.
# The MAIN MENU is reached from its bottom, so the walk is the same whether
# the guest is signed in to RetroAchievements (the menu then opens on that
# row, above GAME SETTINGS) or not. Probed one press at a time on 2026-09-29
# (proofs-307/up-probe.steps): up from the top row lands on an unmarked stop
# with nothing highlighted, the next on BACK, the third on QUIT, and the rows
# above QUIT never move. Three presses to QUIT, not two.
key ret
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot network-settings
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
wait 5
settle
shot wifi-networks
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot wifi-saved-network
key z
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key z
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
wait 3
settle
shot saved-networks
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot forget-network
dismiss-dialogs
